From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 03:20:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] iommu: pkvm-pviommu: report EL2 attach failures

Surface the raw hypervisor status and failing attach stage in the protected
guest.  The public SMCCC status collapses every failure to -EINVAL, hiding
whether route lookup, domain allocation, or device attachment failed.

This is temporary bring-up telemetry for the Orin pKVM debug target.
---
 drivers/iommu/pkvm-pviommu.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/iommu/pkvm-pviommu.c b/drivers/iommu/pkvm-pviommu.c
index b5c25f4101a7..d17105d64613 100644
--- a/drivers/iommu/pkvm-pviommu.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/pkvm-pviommu.c
@@ -252,6 +252,10 @@ static int pviommu_set_dev_pasid(struct iommu_domain *domain,
 				  pv->id, sid, pasid,
 				  pv_domain->id, master->ssid_bits, &res);
 		if (res.a0) {
+			dev_err(dev,
+				"attach_dev sid %u failed: smccc %ld, hyp %ld, stage %lu, endpoint %lu\n",
+				sid, (long)res.a0, (long)res.a1, res.a2,
+				res.a3);
 			ret = smccc_to_linux_ret(res.a0);
 			break;
 		}
-- 
2.51.0

